1
00:01:08,628 --> 00:01:12,468
[3. One and Only Summer]

2
00:01:13,991 --> 00:01:15,266
- Goh Hui Jun.
- Here!

3
00:01:15,266 --> 00:01:16,616
[Episode 3]
[To-do list]

4
00:01:16,616 --> 00:01:17,874
- Kim Gi Nam.
- Yes.

5
00:01:17,874 --> 00:01:18,870
[Collect purses, Christmas in Switzerland,
higher SAT score]

6
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,402
- Kim Jin Mi.
- Here.

7
00:01:20,402 --> 00:01:21,206
[Sung Sae Ryeong]

8
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:22,859
- Kim Hye Won.
- Here.

9
00:01:22,859 --> 00:01:24,178
Sung...

10
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,414
- Oh Yun Beom.
- Here.

11
00:01:34,011 --> 00:01:36,293
- Yu Jin Yeong.
- Here.

12
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:38,974
Lee Na Gyeong.

13
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:40,668
Here.

14
00:01:40,668 --> 00:01:42,436
Lee Won Bae.

15
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:43,711
Here.

16
00:01:44,843 --> 00:01:47,296
- Lee Hyeon Jin.
- Yes, sir.

17
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:51,005
- Lee Il Ho.
- Present.

18
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:54,975
Sung Sae Ryeong's absent today, right?

19
00:01:54,975 --> 00:01:56,884
Why didn't he call on her?

20
00:01:57,591 --> 00:02:00,626
He just skipped right over her, right?

21
00:02:01,478 --> 00:02:04,241
Hey, Jin Mi.
Have you heard from Sung Sae Ryeong at all?

22
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:06,540
No.

23
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:07,915
Nothing.

24
00:02:08,551 --> 00:02:09,814
Listen to this.

25
00:02:09,814 --> 00:02:13,998
This morning,
I overheard my parents say something strange.

26
00:02:13,998 --> 00:02:15,131
What strange thing?

27
00:02:15,131 --> 00:02:16,174
Come on, what is it?

28
00:02:16,174 --> 00:02:18,889
Tell us, tell us! Come on, spit it out!

29
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:21,130
- What?
- Well, it was...

30
00:02:23,031 --> 00:02:25,187
I heard that Sung Sae Ryeong died.

31
00:02:25,187 --> 00:02:27,658
Hey! That's nothing to joke about!

32
00:02:27,658 --> 00:02:29,232
You shouldn't lie about that stuff.

33
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:31,824
I'm not joking, I swear!

34
00:02:31,824 --> 00:02:34,400
- Did you hear about Sung Sae Ryeong?
- Hear what?

35
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:38,202
- Stop lying.
- I'm serious!

36
00:02:38,202 --> 00:02:40,243
What? Who died?

37
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:42,168
She said Sung Sae Ryeong died.

38
00:02:42,168 --> 00:02:43,211
- No way.
- What?

39
00:02:43,211 --> 00:02:45,274
- Are you for real?
- Yeah, I am.

40
00:04:27,811 --> 00:04:29,381
<i>Hi, Yun Ah.</i>

41
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:32,491
<i>It's me, Ha Yeon.</i>

42
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,651
Hi, Ha Yeon!

43
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,569
What number are you calling from?

44
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:44,094
Well, see...

45
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,255
I called because
I don't think I can give you that 50,000 won.

46
00:04:49,874 --> 00:04:50,874
You know,

47
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:54,373
the money that you ordered
Heo Mi Hee to get from me.

48
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,298
I can't give it to you.

49
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,509
<i>W-What did you say?</i>

50
00:05:00,509 --> 00:05:01,885
I'm sorry.

51
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:04,908
Something came up, and I need it.

52
00:05:04,908 --> 00:05:06,640
<i>Hey, Ha Yeon.</i>

53
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,617
I'm Yun Ah.

54
00:05:08,617 --> 00:05:10,268
- Choi Yun Ah.
- Yun Ah!

55
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:11,470
Let's go to the restroom together.

56
00:05:11,470 --> 00:05:13,271
Come on!

57
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:14,856
<i>I know.</i>

58
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:17,047
<i>You're Choi Yun Ah.</i>

59
00:05:17,047 --> 00:05:21,216
And I know you've been using Heo Mi Hee
to bully me,

60
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:27,702
and I know you've been pretending
to be nice to me all this time.

61
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:30,517
<i>I don't see what you're getting at, Ha Yeon.</i>

62
00:05:30,517 --> 00:05:32,761
<i>Is there something going on with you?</i>

63
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:36,953
Yes.

64
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,536
I'm dying today.

65
00:05:40,536 --> 00:05:41,812
<i>What?</i>

66
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:45,601
I just thought I'd call before I die.

67
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:51,226
I figured you had no idea
I knew who you really are.

68
00:05:51,226 --> 00:05:53,853
It started with the sundress.

69
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:55,933
Why would Heo Mi Hee even want it?

70
00:05:55,933 --> 00:05:57,732
<i>As you know,</i>

71
00:05:57,732 --> 00:06:02,042
<i>she has a burn scar on her leg that she's
insecure about, and keeps under long socks.</i>

72
00:06:02,042 --> 00:06:06,306
<i>I've never even seen her wear shorts
outside of school, much less a skirt.</i>

73
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:09,299
<i>So why the sundress?</i>

74
00:06:10,621 --> 00:06:12,299
Ugh...

75
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,597
But, Choi Yun Ah...

76
00:06:18,003 --> 00:06:19,423
I...

77
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:22,711
I still liked you.

78
00:06:23,717 --> 00:06:28,016
I knew you were a cheat,
and I still liked you regardless.

79
00:06:29,264 --> 00:06:30,307
Why?

80
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:36,500
Because you'd at least pretend
to be nice to me.

81
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,939
Pretending to be kind.

82
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:44,552
Pretending that you don't hate me.

83
00:06:44,552 --> 00:06:45,628
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon.

84
00:06:45,628 --> 00:06:48,729
<i>But since I'm dying anyway,</i>
let me give you some advice.

85
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:53,650
Don't ever make anyone go through this again.

86
00:06:56,791 --> 00:07:00,200
Speaking from experience, indirect bullying
is worse than active bullying.

87
00:07:03,029 --> 00:07:04,872
It sucks beyond words.

88
00:07:07,484 --> 00:07:08,842
Wouldn't you agree?

89
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:13,210
You're not just a horrible person,
but a spineless coward as well.

90
00:07:14,938 --> 00:07:16,513
So, Choi Yun Ah,

91
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:19,783
you are, no doubt...

92
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:22,373
the worst person I know of.

93
00:07:22,373 --> 00:07:24,069
I'm telling you in good faith,

94
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:27,302
because I was worried you'd never learn
how horrible you are your whole life.

95
00:07:30,909 --> 00:07:33,740
The biggest tramp in this whole wide world,

96
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:37,121
is no other than you.

97
00:07:37,121 --> 00:07:38,277
<i>Hey!</i>

98
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:57,270
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon!

99
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:41,104
Hey, Babe.

100
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:42,478
Yeah?

101
00:08:42,478 --> 00:08:43,773
Ha Yeon...

102
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:45,108
She...

103
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:49,918
Did she not come home, or did she leave early?

104
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:54,536
Her uniform and book bag are still here,
but her shoes are gone.

105
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:57,913
She must've gone out.

106
00:08:57,913 --> 00:08:59,406
I need to go.

107
00:09:01,124 --> 00:09:03,187
But...

108
00:09:03,187 --> 00:09:06,652
I think... she's gone missing.

109
00:09:07,915 --> 00:09:09,174
Don't you think?

110
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:11,718
What? There's no way.

111
00:09:12,371 --> 00:09:13,757
Call her.

112
00:09:21,311 --> 00:09:25,627
<i>The number you are calling
is temporarily unavailable.</i>

113
00:09:27,087 --> 00:09:30,659
<i>Did you see the text Mom sent you yesterday?</i>

114
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:32,717
<i>No.</i>

115
00:09:32,717 --> 00:09:34,152
<i>Why not?</i>

116
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:37,744
<i>My phone fell in the sea.</i>

117
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:41,638
Seriously...

118
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,091
Who is it?

119
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:55,449
Excuse me, ma'am.

120
00:09:56,346 --> 00:09:57,848
Good morning.

121
00:09:57,848 --> 00:09:59,863
I'm from the Upo District
Women and Juvenile Affairs Division,

122
00:09:59,863 --> 00:10:02,716
Youth Affairs Team 2,
Police Sergeant Choi Wan Jae.

123
00:10:04,229 --> 00:10:07,486
You must be Kim Ha Yeon's caretaker.

124
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,974
Yes, I am, sir.

125
00:10:10,974 --> 00:10:12,317
What's this about?

126
00:10:13,328 --> 00:10:15,090
Is she home right now?

127
00:10:40,223 --> 00:10:44,769
200 meters in one minute and fifty seconds!

128
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,272
That's a new record.

129
00:10:47,272 --> 00:10:48,302
Hey, Yu Gyeom.

130
00:10:48,302 --> 00:10:51,585
You'd easily win the national tournament
with a record like this.

131
00:10:57,574 --> 00:10:58,611
Hey.

132
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:06,124
Are you serious about
just keeping this as a hobby?

133
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:07,409
Yeah, it can't be helped.

134
00:11:07,409 --> 00:11:09,566
Or do you have any other ideas?

135
00:11:10,169 --> 00:11:12,489
Don't tell this to your grandfather.

136
00:11:12,489 --> 00:11:13,912
Come here, boy.

137
00:11:14,549 --> 00:11:15,745
Come on.

138
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:22,778
You should persuade him yourself.

139
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:27,212
I failed, but I really do think you'll manage!

140
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,732
Come on!

141
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:33,067
Just try it once, please?

142
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:35,169
I'm not asking you to try it twice,
just bring it up once!

143
00:11:35,169 --> 00:11:36,252
Just this once!

144
00:11:36,252 --> 00:11:38,157
My father tried that, too.

145
00:11:38,157 --> 00:11:40,680
"Just this once," and "Just one more time."

146
00:11:41,618 --> 00:11:45,607
He made it into the national team,
and into the Olympics,

147
00:11:45,607 --> 00:11:48,001
and became the first person from Asia
to make it into the finals.

148
00:11:48,917 --> 00:11:50,308
Hey, Teach.

149
00:11:50,308 --> 00:11:52,991
Do you know what happened to him after that?

150
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,225
He forfeited.

151
00:11:57,225 --> 00:11:59,491
He forfeited after making it to the finals.

152
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:05,242
I wasn't born yet, so I didn't know,
but I heard it was a whole thing.

153
00:12:06,004 --> 00:12:09,579
He became the punching bag
of the whole country.

154
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,565
So, sir.

155
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:14,150
I'd rather not.

156
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:17,137
I don't want to compete
if I'm going to end up like my dad.

157
00:12:17,137 --> 00:12:19,530
Nobody wants to be the national punching bag.

158
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:22,597
Then you'll just have to see it to the end,
unlike him.

159
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:24,823
Just this once.

160
00:12:24,823 --> 00:12:26,975
Cho Yu Gyeom!

161
00:12:31,751 --> 00:12:37,364
We just want to know what you were doing
between 8 p.m. and midnight yesterday.

162
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:41,219
I was at the lighthouse.

163
00:12:41,219 --> 00:12:43,121
The lighthouse?

164
00:12:43,121 --> 00:12:44,847
The lighthouse by the Upo Country Club.

165
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:46,724
Who were you with?

166
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:47,822
I was alone.

167
00:12:47,822 --> 00:12:51,938
Did you meet Sung Sae Ryeong by any chance?

168
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:52,970
No, I didn't.

169
00:12:52,970 --> 00:12:54,624
What about Kim Ha Yeon?

170
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,283
No.

171
00:12:57,283 --> 00:12:59,479
Then why were you there?

172
00:12:59,479 --> 00:13:00,665
At night, no less?

173
00:13:02,394 --> 00:13:03,966
I was waiting for someone.

174
00:13:03,966 --> 00:13:05,035
Who?

175
00:13:05,035 --> 00:13:07,556
- Was it Sung Sae Ryeong?
- No, Kim Ha Yeon.

176
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:11,860
By the way,
I don't see why you're asking me all this.

177
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,876
What's wrong with Ha Yeon?

178
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:17,826
She has been missing since last night.

179
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:19,869
Ha Yeon's missing?

180
00:13:19,869 --> 00:13:22,969
Why? Did something bad happen to her?

181
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:24,120
No, no.

182
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:27,010
We're still trying to figure out what happened.

183
00:13:27,682 --> 00:13:29,642
But this is peculiar.

184
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:32,488
Are you more interested in Kim Ha Yeon?

185
00:13:32,488 --> 00:13:37,818
I heard Sung Sae Ryeong was your girlfriend,
but you seem disinterested in her whereabouts.

186
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:44,184
Did Sae Ryeong...

187
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:47,077
die, or something?

188
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:07,198
Ma'am, I don't speak sign language.

189
00:14:07,198 --> 00:14:08,541
My granddaughter.

190
00:14:08,541 --> 00:14:11,720
- I'm sorry, I don't know sign language!
- My granddaughter!

191
00:14:17,428 --> 00:14:19,404
<i>Sung Sae Ryeong is...</i>

192
00:14:23,196 --> 00:14:25,964
Your granddaughter is awake now.

193
00:14:25,964 --> 00:14:27,988
You must've been so worried, ma'am.

194
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:37,951
<i>alive.</i>

195
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:42,632
She injured her head pretty badly, though.

196
00:14:42,632 --> 00:14:44,231
All's well if she's alive.

197
00:14:44,231 --> 00:14:45,947
Well, the problem is...

198
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:01,381
<i>Yes, this is 112, emergency services.</i>

199
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,567
<i>How did you get hurt?</i>

200
00:15:05,567 --> 00:15:07,380
<i>Can you speak, miss?</i>

201
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:10,624
<i>Cho Yu Gyeom...</i>

202
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:12,458
<i>Yes, miss?</i>

203
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:16,263
<i>Cho Yu Gyeom.</i>

204
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,722
Sung Sae Ryeong

205
00:15:18,722 --> 00:15:21,952
said that you, Cho Yu Gyeom, hit her
and caused her injury,

206
00:15:21,952 --> 00:15:24,298
and directly informed the police about it.

207
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:26,614
That's why we're here.

208
00:15:26,614 --> 00:15:27,909
That lunatic.

209
00:15:28,564 --> 00:15:29,621
What?

210
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,602
Listen here.

211
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,697
Sung Sae Ryeong is a complete lunatic.

212
00:15:36,697 --> 00:15:38,136
Did you know that?

213
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:43,025
We still have to investigate it.

214
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:47,479
She's not in a condition to give us
any straight answers as of now.

215
00:15:47,479 --> 00:15:52,192
We'd like you to accompany us to the precinct.

216
00:15:52,192 --> 00:15:55,225
Come with us to the station, please.

217
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:04,651
<i>Is that you, Jung Yeon?</i>

218
00:16:04,651 --> 00:16:05,726
<i>Jung Yeon!</i>

219
00:16:05,726 --> 00:16:07,257
<i>Have you seen Ha Yeon?</i>

220
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:09,511
No.

221
00:16:10,595 --> 00:16:11,842
I haven't.

222
00:16:11,842 --> 00:16:13,807
<i>She's gone missing!</i>

223
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:16,083
<i>That unhinged brat
apparently beat up some local girl!</i>

224
00:16:16,083 --> 00:16:17,884
<i>And she did it with some boy!</i>

225
00:16:17,884 --> 00:16:20,562
<i>She's seriously driving me crazy!</i>

226
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:22,537
<i>That unruly brat of a girl!</i>

227
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:26,167
Mom.

228
00:16:26,167 --> 00:16:27,390
What?

229
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:29,238
What now?

230
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:33,728
I think she came by our home in Seoul.

231
00:16:33,728 --> 00:16:34,911
What?

232
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:36,056
When?

233
00:16:36,954 --> 00:16:38,498
Well...

234
00:16:56,933 --> 00:17:00,285
I think I heard someone come in
while I was taking a nap.

235
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,728
I think that was her going into her room.

236
00:17:03,728 --> 00:17:05,071
You.

237
00:17:05,071 --> 00:17:07,030
Do you really have no idea where she went?

238
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:09,100
<i>- She...</i>
- I honestly don't know.

239
00:17:11,906 --> 00:17:13,741
<i>Hello?</i>

240
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:15,829
<i>Hello? Jung Yeon!</i>

241
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:21,624
<i>Mom, Dad.</i>

242
00:17:21,624 --> 00:17:24,085
<i>Thank you for raising me.</i>

243
00:17:24,085 --> 00:17:25,908
<i>I wish you a happy life as well, Jung Yeon.</i>

244
00:17:25,908 --> 00:17:30,118
<i>I heard people tell their family
that they love them before they die.</i>

245
00:17:30,118 --> 00:17:34,080
<i>But I don't recall receiving any love,
so I have none to give back.</i>

246
00:17:35,142 --> 00:17:37,819
<i>However, I truly do feel sorry
for Sung Sae Ryeong.</i>

247
00:17:38,641 --> 00:17:40,346
<i>Tell her...</i>

248
00:17:41,269 --> 00:17:43,578
<i>that I said I'm sorry.</i>

249
00:17:46,402 --> 00:17:47,504
Mom.

250
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:53,796
I think... she wrote us a goodbye letter.

251
00:17:53,796 --> 00:17:58,264
<i>She wrote that she wants us to tell
Sung Sae Ryeong she's sorry.</i>

252
00:17:59,593 --> 00:18:00,751
What?

253
00:18:00,751 --> 00:18:02,387
What are you saying?

254
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,423
<i>Oh my goodness!</i>

255
00:18:04,423 --> 00:18:05,848
<i>No way, did she really?</i>

256
00:18:05,848 --> 00:18:08,067
<i>Did she actually assault
that Sung Sae Ryeong girl?</i>

257
00:18:09,529 --> 00:18:11,492
<i>The police came by this morning!</i>

258
00:18:11,492 --> 00:18:13,875
Some girl named Sae Ryeong reported her.

259
00:18:13,875 --> 00:18:16,124
She said Ha Yeon hit her!

260
00:18:16,124 --> 00:18:17,930
And that boy, the boy!

261
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:21,616
The boy who did it with her is already
at the police station now!

262
00:18:21,616 --> 00:18:23,137
Unbelievable.

263
00:18:23,137 --> 00:18:24,253
Think about that.

264
00:18:24,253 --> 00:18:26,511
Ha Yeon isn't the type to hit anyone.

265
00:18:26,511 --> 00:18:27,839
It makes no sense!

266
00:18:27,839 --> 00:18:30,709
She's more the type to get beaten up.

267
00:18:30,709 --> 00:18:32,982
She'd never hit anyone!

268
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:35,652
Jung Yeon...

269
00:18:35,652 --> 00:18:38,191
If this actually turns into a case,
there'll be a School Violence Committee trial!

270
00:18:38,191 --> 00:18:40,786
They'll put it in her official school report!

271
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:43,622
<i>She's already struggling
to make it into a university in Seoul!</i>

272
00:18:43,622 --> 00:18:45,626
<i>Everything's a disaster!</i>

273
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:48,059
<i>I should teach her a lesson!</i>

274
00:18:48,059 --> 00:18:49,654
<i>How dare she disappear
after doing something so stupid?</i>

275
00:18:49,654 --> 00:18:51,529
<i>Where the hell is she?</i>

276
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:54,254
Mom.

277
00:18:54,254 --> 00:18:55,599
<i>What now?</i>

278
00:18:55,599 --> 00:18:56,896
What!

279
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,399
She said she's going to die.

280
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:03,324
<i>What?</i>

281
00:19:04,352 --> 00:19:07,482
Whether she hit someone or not isn't the point!

282
00:19:08,196 --> 00:19:11,894
The point is, she left a goodbye letter
saying she's going to die, Mom!

283
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,895
She's going to kill herself.

284
00:19:18,102 --> 00:19:20,291
Isn't that what matters the most right now?

285
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:26,659
Then...

286
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:29,379
Where...

287
00:19:29,379 --> 00:19:31,399
Where is she right now?

288
00:19:45,101 --> 00:19:48,583
<i>I can't overdose,
since I can't get my hands on pills.</i>

289
00:19:48,583 --> 00:19:52,817
<i>I can't run into traffic, because I'd feel bad
for the person who ends up hitting me.</i>

290
00:19:52,817 --> 00:19:56,238
<i>Nor am I brave enough to jump.</i>

291
00:19:56,238 --> 00:19:58,546
<i>And drowning in the sea here...</i>

292
00:20:12,868 --> 00:20:15,358
<i>Drowning in the sea here is...</i>

293
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,711
I killed a person...

294
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:35,396
but I'm still scared of dying myself!

295
00:20:49,999 --> 00:20:51,646
Hey, you there.

296
00:20:53,169 --> 00:20:54,510
Hey, you!

297
00:21:04,175 --> 00:21:05,597
Hey, girl.

298
00:21:05,597 --> 00:21:07,557
Why are you crying?

299
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:09,053
What's wrong?

300
00:21:09,686 --> 00:21:11,227
Is something the matter?

301
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:19,737
What do you mean?

302
00:21:19,737 --> 00:21:22,990
Just explain it to me, come on.

303
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:26,831
So he's at the police station right now.

304
00:21:26,831 --> 00:21:28,411
The police...

305
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,756
went to Yu Gyeom's school.

306
00:21:31,756 --> 00:21:34,878
If something happened to him,
the school should have handled it.

307
00:21:34,878 --> 00:21:37,087
Why did they take him to the police station?

308
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,130
That's the thing, Father.

309
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:43,046
The victim reported it to the police herself.

310
00:21:43,983 --> 00:21:46,791
So the police have to
question the witnesses first.

311
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,433
Who was it?

312
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:50,480
Pardon me?

313
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,849
Who is this supposed victim?

314
00:21:52,849 --> 00:21:54,967
Who the hell is it?

315
00:22:06,367 --> 00:22:07,411
Here you go.

316
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:09,650
Drink it.

317
00:22:09,650 --> 00:22:11,365
It'll warm you up.

318
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:15,182
By the way, if I may ask...

319
00:22:15,182 --> 00:22:16,988
Do you have nowhere to stay?

320
00:22:19,157 --> 00:22:20,654
Well?

321
00:22:20,654 --> 00:22:22,306
You could stay at my place if you'd like.

322
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:27,096
I'm not a bad person, I promise.

323
00:22:27,096 --> 00:22:28,158
Hey.

324
00:22:28,158 --> 00:22:30,993
Have you ever seen anyone as pretty as me
turn out to be a bad person?

325
00:22:36,522 --> 00:22:37,804
I guess you have.

326
00:22:40,249 --> 00:22:44,074
By the way, why were you crying back there?

327
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:47,313
Could you tell me in secret?

328
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:50,565
It's okay.

329
00:22:50,565 --> 00:22:52,103
You can tell me.

330
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:03,383
I...

331
00:23:22,237 --> 00:23:23,432
Sir.

332
00:23:30,864 --> 00:23:32,786
I see.

333
00:23:32,786 --> 00:23:34,844
So you wanted to die?

334
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:37,626
Yes.

335
00:23:39,293 --> 00:23:40,993
Then...

336
00:23:40,993 --> 00:23:43,004
Do you want me to help you die?

337
00:23:44,577 --> 00:23:46,620
Can you do that for me?

338
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:47,718
Sure!

339
00:23:47,718 --> 00:23:49,582
Of course I can do that.

340
00:23:49,582 --> 00:23:51,587
You just need to get your hands on some pills.

341
00:23:51,587 --> 00:23:54,605
It's the least painful method, right?

342
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:03,129
Places like this...
have lots of pills going around.

343
00:24:06,153 --> 00:24:08,100
But I'm actually curious.

344
00:24:08,100 --> 00:24:10,336
Why do you want to die?

345
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:18,442
Sung Sae Ryeong?

346
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:22,900
Yes, of course I know you.

347
00:24:26,965 --> 00:24:31,178
You're the girl Yu Gyeom is seeing, right?

348
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:32,220
Sir.

349
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:35,093
- Yu Gyeom hit me.
- Is that so?

350
00:24:35,093 --> 00:24:37,068
And you reported it to the police?

351
00:24:37,068 --> 00:24:40,169
- Yes, sir, Cho Yu Gyeom--
- Little lass.

352
00:24:42,022 --> 00:24:47,039
People are useless when they grow old.

353
00:24:47,039 --> 00:24:49,571
But God is fair to all.

354
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:52,868
God bestows a gift upon the old.

355
00:24:52,868 --> 00:24:55,229
What could it be, you may ask?

356
00:24:55,229 --> 00:24:58,539
An eye, it is, that can see through anything.

357
00:24:58,539 --> 00:25:00,722
An eye for discerning things.

358
00:25:01,973 --> 00:25:05,748
I hear that your family is quite wealthy.

359
00:25:05,748 --> 00:25:08,117
So where are your wealthy parents?

360
00:25:08,117 --> 00:25:11,708
Where are they, when their beloved daughter
is hurt and lying in a hospital bed?

361
00:25:11,708 --> 00:25:15,194
My parents are a bit busy at the moment.

362
00:25:15,194 --> 00:25:17,076
Is that so?

363
00:25:17,808 --> 00:25:20,660
Your father is a politician, yes?

364
00:25:21,395 --> 00:25:24,712
Sung Sae Ryeong, from the Sung family.

365
00:25:24,712 --> 00:25:27,081
Of course I know the Sung family.

366
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:29,627
But, if I may recall...

367
00:25:29,627 --> 00:25:33,109
no one in the Sung family
has ever become a politician.

368
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:37,858
There was, however, a Sung family member
who was a sea dog.

369
00:25:37,858 --> 00:25:42,972
He'd sail around here in his dinghy,
and sometimes he'd come into town.

370
00:25:42,972 --> 00:25:45,141
I haven't seen him for some time now.

371
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:50,523
You see, there...

372
00:25:51,172 --> 00:25:54,479
There was this deaf and mute woman
in the Sung family,

373
00:25:54,479 --> 00:25:56,584
that mothered the sea dog.

374
00:26:00,983 --> 00:26:03,640
I don't know who that is.
That's not my grandma.

375
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:06,733
I didn't say anything
about her being your grandmother,

376
00:26:06,733 --> 00:26:09,086
I said she was the sea dog's mother.

377
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:21,741
Your incessant lying has stripped you
of the ability to discern lies from the truth!

378
00:26:21,741 --> 00:26:25,102
- Excuse me.
- It's a disease, it is!

379
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,342
I murdered someone.

380
00:26:40,349 --> 00:26:42,184
Is that so?

381
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:43,634
You?

382
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:46,209
Yes.

383
00:26:46,209 --> 00:26:47,883
Right...

384
00:26:48,774 --> 00:26:50,263
I see.

385
00:26:50,263 --> 00:26:52,338
I get why you'd want to die.

386
00:26:53,070 --> 00:26:54,822
Okay.

387
00:26:54,822 --> 00:26:59,006
If you're really in that much turmoil,
I'll get you some pills.

388
00:27:03,205 --> 00:27:05,457
It will cost you a pretty penny, though.

389
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:07,209
Is that okay with you?

390
00:27:07,209 --> 00:27:09,837
How much will it be?

391
00:27:09,837 --> 00:27:11,588
Well, I don't know.

392
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:14,979
Probably about ten million won.

393
00:27:23,809 --> 00:27:25,891
Hey, you, cutie pie.

394
00:27:25,891 --> 00:27:29,138
There's a price for everything, even dying.

395
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:36,544
But I don't have that much money.

396
00:27:36,544 --> 00:27:37,576
Girl.

397
00:27:37,576 --> 00:27:39,929
You're going to die anyway.

398
00:27:39,929 --> 00:27:42,925
So all you need to do is call someone
and ask to borrow the money.

399
00:27:42,925 --> 00:27:45,060
Then you'll be free to die.

400
00:27:45,060 --> 00:27:46,476
No need to pay them back.

401
00:27:46,476 --> 00:27:48,055
- Okay?
- What?

402
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:53,435
But I don't have a phone with me.

403
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:56,675
You're silly.

404
00:27:56,675 --> 00:27:59,500
Everybody has a phone these days.

405
00:27:59,500 --> 00:28:00,835
You're lying, aren't you?

406
00:28:01,559 --> 00:28:03,348
No, I'm telling you the truth.

407
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:06,020
My phone fell into the sea and broke.

408
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:08,705
I see.

409
00:28:09,563 --> 00:28:10,933
Well, then.

410
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:13,666
Hey, Hee Ji!

411
00:28:20,824 --> 00:28:21,849
There.

412
00:28:22,989 --> 00:28:29,723
Take this, step outside, find the
payphone nearby, and make that call.

413
00:28:29,723 --> 00:28:30,953
You can do that, right?

414
00:28:30,953 --> 00:28:35,189
You've made up your mind to die,
so how hard can it be to make a call?

415
00:28:35,189 --> 00:28:36,217
Right?

416
00:28:51,104 --> 00:28:53,370
Sung Sae Ryeong.

417
00:28:58,593 --> 00:29:02,336
Did Yu Gyeom really hit you?

418
00:29:02,336 --> 00:29:05,139
He can't hit anyone.

419
00:29:05,139 --> 00:29:08,248
- No, sir, he definitely--
- I...

420
00:29:08,248 --> 00:29:11,041
didn't teach him to do that.

421
00:29:11,041 --> 00:29:14,294
I never taught him to do that.

422
00:29:14,294 --> 00:29:19,398
My boy, Yu Gyeom,
can't do something that I never taught him!

423
00:29:19,398 --> 00:29:21,802
You must be delusional, sir,

424
00:29:21,802 --> 00:29:25,037
- because Yu Gyeom did actually--
- Hush, now.

425
00:29:32,396 --> 00:29:35,065
To ruin his life so utterly and completely,

426
00:29:35,065 --> 00:29:38,022
stopping anyone else from
swooping in and taking him,

427
00:29:38,022 --> 00:29:39,985
so that you can eat him up?

428
00:29:41,363 --> 00:29:42,644
Isn't that your plan?

429
00:29:42,644 --> 00:29:46,340
- Isn't that your grand scheme, your life goal?
- No, it isn't! It's not!

430
00:29:48,704 --> 00:29:52,374
You are so young, so supple and pretty.

431
00:29:52,374 --> 00:29:55,120
So how did you end up like this?

432
00:29:55,120 --> 00:29:56,294
Listen to me, sir--

433
00:29:56,294 --> 00:29:59,216
I'm not asking for much.

434
00:29:59,216 --> 00:30:02,653
Go to the police, and tell them the truth.

435
00:30:02,653 --> 00:30:05,875
The truth, and only the truth.

436
00:30:05,875 --> 00:30:10,808
- I'm saying that the truth is that he--
- And you'll get to live here.

437
00:30:10,808 --> 00:30:13,772
I'll just pretend nothing happened.

438
00:30:13,772 --> 00:30:16,914
But if you keep acting so stubborn...

439
00:30:17,562 --> 00:30:21,400
your grand life plan
won't ever come to fruition.

440
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:22,758
Why?

441
00:30:22,758 --> 00:30:26,087
Because you and your grandmother...

442
00:30:26,087 --> 00:30:29,396
will be exiled from this town
before any of it can come true.

443
00:30:30,376 --> 00:30:31,809
Sir...

444
00:30:37,632 --> 00:30:40,374
Do you have anywhere else to go?

445
00:30:41,548 --> 00:30:46,625
You're a bright little thing,
so I'll take it that you understood me.

446
00:30:58,723 --> 00:30:59,873
Let's go.

447
00:31:14,664 --> 00:31:16,374
What are you hesitating for?

448
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,203
Make the call.

449
00:31:20,409 --> 00:31:24,643
[Payphone]

450
00:31:43,360 --> 00:31:44,700
Hello?

451
00:31:45,664 --> 00:31:48,013
Hey, Jung Yeon.

452
00:31:48,806 --> 00:31:50,304
It's me.

453
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:53,605
Do you have money?

454
00:31:55,497 --> 00:31:57,155
Money? Why?

455
00:31:57,155 --> 00:31:59,278
<i>I just need it.</i>

456
00:32:02,212 --> 00:32:03,728
How much?

457
00:32:03,728 --> 00:32:06,603
[Payphone]
As much as you can scrounge up.

458
00:32:09,386 --> 00:32:10,723
Like...

459
00:32:14,683 --> 00:32:17,685
about ten million won.

460
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:23,318
All right. I'll do it.

461
00:32:23,318 --> 00:32:24,344
<i>What?</i>

462
00:32:25,026 --> 00:32:26,488
I'll lend it to you.

463
00:32:27,779 --> 00:32:29,595
<i>Wait, seriously?</i>

464
00:32:29,595 --> 00:32:31,465
<i>Think it through.
You don't have that much money.</i>

465
00:32:31,465 --> 00:32:33,106
I do.

466
00:32:33,106 --> 00:32:34,202
[Mom, could you track this number?]

467
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:38,231
[Ha Yeon just called me from it.]
But, well... It might take an hour or so.

468
00:32:38,231 --> 00:32:39,454
Is that okay?

469
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:41,797
An hour?

470
00:32:41,797 --> 00:32:43,217
<i>Yes, an hour.</i>

471
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:48,594
<i>Mom, could you track this number?</i>

472
00:32:48,594 --> 00:32:50,802
<i>Ha Yeon just called me from it.</i>

473
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:51,833
Sergeant Lee.

474
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:53,008
Yes, sir.

475
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:57,267
Run this number through the system.

476
00:32:57,267 --> 00:32:58,500
Yes, sir.

477
00:33:03,371 --> 00:33:06,355
I might not need it if it'll take an hour.

478
00:33:07,642 --> 00:33:08,945
<i>What?</i>

479
00:33:08,945 --> 00:33:10,366
<i>You might not need it?</i>

480
00:33:10,366 --> 00:33:12,073
Well...

481
00:33:12,073 --> 00:33:13,894
No, I mean, I'll need it.

482
00:33:13,894 --> 00:33:15,320
Then give me the account number.

483
00:33:22,086 --> 00:33:23,730
<i>Modu Bank...</i>

484
00:33:25,462 --> 00:33:27,336
<i>3333...</i>

485
00:33:27,336 --> 00:33:29,521
Hey! Hee Ji.

486
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,195
Wait a moment.

487
00:33:31,195 --> 00:33:32,581
She's making a call.

488
00:33:35,057 --> 00:33:36,912
So I should transfer it here?

489
00:33:40,602 --> 00:33:41,894
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon.

490
00:33:44,064 --> 00:33:47,189
By the way, why are you suddenly
so eager to lend me money?

491
00:33:53,907 --> 00:33:56,201
You asked me to, no?

492
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:58,023
<i>But are you serious?</i>

493
00:33:58,023 --> 00:34:00,204
<i>Think it through.
You don't have that much money.</i>

494
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:02,197
Do you want me to, or not?

495
00:34:04,445 --> 00:34:05,981
<i>Never mind.</i>

496
00:34:07,003 --> 00:34:08,032
<i>I'm hanging up.</i>

497
00:34:08,032 --> 00:34:09,296
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon.

498
00:34:11,672 --> 00:34:13,420
Where are you right now?

499
00:34:15,345 --> 00:34:16,881
Why do you ask?

500
00:34:16,881 --> 00:34:18,383
Just... where are you?

501
00:34:20,895 --> 00:34:22,816
You're in Seoul, aren't you?

502
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:28,038
Yeah.

503
00:34:28,038 --> 00:34:29,214
I am.

504
00:34:32,057 --> 00:34:34,408
Is that why you agreed to lend me money?

505
00:34:34,408 --> 00:34:35,484
<i>Yes.</i>

506
00:34:36,264 --> 00:34:37,486
<i>So?</i>

507
00:34:40,537 --> 00:34:42,669
Do you want me to die?

508
00:34:47,711 --> 00:34:49,927
I wouldn't say that I want you to.

509
00:34:51,384 --> 00:34:53,714
But I don't care enough to stop you.

510
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:57,418
<i>If you don't care,
why do you want to know where I am?</i>

511
00:34:57,418 --> 00:35:00,487
<i>You're trying to track me down, aren't you?</i>

512
00:35:00,487 --> 00:35:01,642
Hey.

513
00:35:03,103 --> 00:35:05,419
I'd prefer it if you died, too, okay?

514
00:35:09,443 --> 00:35:11,066
What?

515
00:35:11,066 --> 00:35:13,482
I said, I'd prefer it if you died, too.

516
00:35:15,634 --> 00:35:17,429
Let's be honest.

517
00:35:17,429 --> 00:35:20,271
I'm not technically lending you money, am I?

518
00:35:20,271 --> 00:35:23,183
I'm just donating all my money to let you die.

519
00:35:23,834 --> 00:35:27,212
Don't you think I deserve to know
where you are, at least?

520
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:32,191
Damn it!

521
00:35:32,191 --> 00:35:36,633
I need to know where you are
so that I can collect your corpse!

522
00:35:37,391 --> 00:35:38,942
<i>Where the hell are you?</i>

523
00:35:43,904 --> 00:35:44,904
I'm...

524
00:35:47,066 --> 00:35:49,057
I am at...

525
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:53,746
A payphone near Gorae Port.

526
00:35:53,746 --> 00:35:56,749
We just informed the nearby precinct.

527
00:35:56,749 --> 00:36:00,018
We'll also track the bank account,
so we'll find her soon enough.

528
00:36:01,465 --> 00:36:02,841
Thank you, sir.

529
00:36:03,599 --> 00:36:06,463
And your son is in Seoul right now,
is that correct?

530
00:36:07,244 --> 00:36:09,066
Yes, sir, he's...

531
00:36:09,066 --> 00:36:10,242
He's in Seoul.

532
00:36:10,242 --> 00:36:14,516
Well, judging by the fact that your daughter
is asking for money out of nowhere...

533
00:36:16,491 --> 00:36:20,539
You see, there's a big human
trafficking ring right around that area.

534
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:24,105
We suspect that she may have
come into contact with one of them.

535
00:36:24,105 --> 00:36:26,888
Of course, it's too soon to say for sure.

536
00:36:27,769 --> 00:36:30,945
But you should warn your son
to stay away at all costs.

537
00:36:30,945 --> 00:36:33,741
It may be dangerous for him
if he goes there, too.

538
00:36:33,741 --> 00:36:36,226
He's pretty young as well, isn't he?

539
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:39,636
He is.

540
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:51,283
You're heading to Gorae Port, yes?

541
00:36:51,283 --> 00:36:52,421
I am.

542
00:36:52,421 --> 00:36:53,857
By the way, sir?

543
00:36:53,857 --> 00:36:56,086
I'm in a hurry. Could you get me there quickly?

544
00:36:56,086 --> 00:36:57,988
Yeah, sure thing.

545
00:37:00,019 --> 00:37:01,406
So.

546
00:37:01,406 --> 00:37:04,463
When is your brother going to
transfer the money?

547
00:37:05,793 --> 00:37:07,871
He said in an hour or so.

548
00:37:09,811 --> 00:37:12,142
Why would it take so long?

549
00:37:12,142 --> 00:37:14,399
He just needs to transfer
the money from his account.

550
00:37:14,399 --> 00:37:16,548
It shouldn't take more than two seconds.

551
00:37:16,548 --> 00:37:18,236
I overheard them talking.

552
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:19,696
What was it you said?

553
00:37:19,696 --> 00:37:22,072
The money is scattered
across multiple accounts, or something?

554
00:37:22,072 --> 00:37:23,569
Yes.

555
00:37:23,569 --> 00:37:26,414
He said he needs to go to the bank himself.

556
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:29,296
Is that so?

557
00:37:30,165 --> 00:37:32,177
Well, then, Ha Yeong.

558
00:37:32,177 --> 00:37:34,487
Excuse me, I...

559
00:37:34,487 --> 00:37:37,380
I'm Ha Yeon.

560
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:39,233
Yeah, sure.

561
00:37:39,233 --> 00:37:40,907
Ha Yeon.

562
00:37:42,366 --> 00:37:44,551
Can you take your clothes off?

563
00:37:53,562 --> 00:37:55,020
What?

564
00:37:55,020 --> 00:37:57,901
As you can see here...

565
00:37:57,901 --> 00:38:02,994
Sung Sae Ryeong and Kim Ha Yeon walk this way,

566
00:38:02,994 --> 00:38:05,424
and the time is around 9:24 p.m.

567
00:38:05,424 --> 00:38:06,826
Yes.

568
00:38:06,826 --> 00:38:08,411
And this here...

569
00:38:08,411 --> 00:38:11,312
is the footage of Cho Yu Gyeom
heading toward the lighthouse.

570
00:38:11,312 --> 00:38:15,793
As you can see, the time is 9:24 p.m.

571
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:16,849
And?

572
00:38:16,849 --> 00:38:18,803
Well, so...

573
00:38:18,803 --> 00:38:23,098
That would mean that, at the same time,
Sung Sae Ryeong and Kim Ha Yeon went this way,

574
00:38:23,098 --> 00:38:26,069
and Cho Yu Gyeom went that way.

575
00:38:26,679 --> 00:38:28,515
I'm sure you already know,

576
00:38:28,515 --> 00:38:32,674
but there's some distance between
the rice fields here and the lighthouse there.

577
00:38:32,674 --> 00:38:35,938
It would still take more than half an hour
to travel, even on a bike.

578
00:38:35,938 --> 00:38:37,436
What I'm saying is,

579
00:38:37,436 --> 00:38:43,116
what Sung Sae Ryeong is claiming is
highly improbable, to say the least.

580
00:38:43,911 --> 00:38:47,495
So can I take Yu Gyeom home now?

581
00:38:47,495 --> 00:38:51,278
- Yes, of course. We're sorry for the hassle.
- No worries, sir.

582
00:38:51,278 --> 00:38:53,994
- We should thank you for your service.
- No, it's fine.

583
00:38:53,994 --> 00:38:56,523
- Yu Gyeom!
- What about Kim Ha Yeon?

584
00:38:57,252 --> 00:38:59,908
- Pardon?
- So where's Kim Ha Yeon?

585
00:38:59,908 --> 00:39:02,479
You said she's gone missing, didn't you?

586
00:39:02,479 --> 00:39:03,550
Did you find her?

587
00:39:03,550 --> 00:39:06,981
Well, we're still working on it.

588
00:39:06,981 --> 00:39:08,567
Sergeant Choi, a moment, please.

589
00:39:08,567 --> 00:39:09,936
Excuse me.

590
00:39:11,224 --> 00:39:13,977
We have a location for Kim Ha Yeon, sir.

591
00:39:13,977 --> 00:39:15,715
She's near Gorae Port.

592
00:39:15,715 --> 00:39:17,427
Or so it seems.

593
00:39:19,232 --> 00:39:22,372
She seems to be held hostage
by that trafficking ring.

594
00:39:22,372 --> 00:39:25,280
So maybe we should reach out first, and...

595
00:39:25,280 --> 00:39:27,189
Hey, Yu Gyeom!

596
00:39:27,189 --> 00:39:28,755
Yu Gyeom!

597
00:39:29,549 --> 00:39:30,789
Well, Ha Yeon?

598
00:39:31,697 --> 00:39:33,298
I'm asking you a question.

599
00:39:33,298 --> 00:39:35,430
Can you take your clothes off, or not?

600
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:43,608
W-Why do you ask?

601
00:39:43,608 --> 00:39:45,732
Oh, come on!

602
00:39:45,732 --> 00:39:49,307
Your brother hasn't transferred the money yet.

603
00:39:50,810 --> 00:39:54,473
But it hasn't been an hour yet, and...

604
00:39:55,342 --> 00:39:58,231
You know what, I don't want the pills anymore.

605
00:40:00,648 --> 00:40:04,235
It's too late now, Ha Yeon.

606
00:40:04,235 --> 00:40:10,120
The moment you said you wanted those pills,
we already got the pills.

607
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:14,120
It cost us a fortune to get them.

608
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:17,651
But how much have you paid us so far?

609
00:40:17,651 --> 00:40:19,189
Twenty...

610
00:40:19,189 --> 00:40:20,526
Thirty...

611
00:40:22,898 --> 00:40:24,913
What is this?

612
00:40:26,507 --> 00:40:29,009
I told you they're worth ten million won!

613
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:31,226
But you gave me 236,000 won, and that's it?

614
00:40:31,226 --> 00:40:34,098
This won't do, don't you think?

615
00:40:34,098 --> 00:40:35,411
I see that, yeah.

616
00:40:35,411 --> 00:40:38,335
So you can just have that, and I'll just...

617
00:40:40,813 --> 00:40:42,640
In here...

618
00:40:42,640 --> 00:40:46,648
You can't take your words back
once you let them out.

619
00:40:48,786 --> 00:40:51,306
Just pay us for the pills.

620
00:40:51,306 --> 00:40:54,160
We don't give a damn if you
actually take them or not.

621
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:57,350
But! We already secured the pills.

622
00:40:57,350 --> 00:40:59,456
So you'll have to pay for them.

623
00:40:59,456 --> 00:41:00,804
Do you follow?

624
00:41:00,804 --> 00:41:03,378
But you're a little short on money.

625
00:41:03,378 --> 00:41:06,881
That's why I'm asking you to undress.

626
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:09,182
Is it so hard to do?

627
00:41:09,182 --> 00:41:11,159
All you need to do is raise your arms,

628
00:41:11,159 --> 00:41:14,120
- and roll your clothes up.
- No!

629
00:41:15,277 --> 00:41:18,265
I really don't feel comfortable
getting undressed.

630
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,772
Ha Yeon.

631
00:41:22,772 --> 00:41:24,732
I'm a woman.

632
00:41:24,732 --> 00:41:28,319
Girls go to public baths together all the time.

633
00:41:28,319 --> 00:41:30,416
Just think of it as that.

634
00:41:30,416 --> 00:41:34,704
Take off your clothes for a little while,
and you can put them back on.

635
00:41:36,202 --> 00:41:37,724
I'll give you the money.

636
00:41:37,724 --> 00:41:42,327
You can have it when my brother transfers it,
but please, I can't take my clothes off.

637
00:41:42,327 --> 00:41:43,400
Hey.

638
00:41:45,172 --> 00:41:47,924
Are you sure you can get me 10 million won?

639
00:41:48,777 --> 00:41:52,315
Exactly 10 million, and not a coin less?

640
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:57,494
My brother said he'd send about 8 million won.

641
00:41:57,494 --> 00:41:59,516
So what about the other 2 million?

642
00:42:01,410 --> 00:42:02,970
But the...

643
00:42:02,970 --> 00:42:05,292
The 236,000 won that I gave you...

644
00:42:05,292 --> 00:42:10,455
All right, then what about
the other 1,764,000 won?

645
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:20,762
I'm asking because I can give you a discount,
if only you would take your clothes off!

646
00:42:22,582 --> 00:42:24,773
I really don't want to...

647
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:35,483
Well, then.

648
00:42:41,017 --> 00:42:43,077
I'll give you 10 minutes.

649
00:42:43,077 --> 00:42:46,230
If you're still fully clothed
after the 10 minutes pass,

650
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:48,936
I'll get them off
if I have to beat them off of you.

651
00:42:48,936 --> 00:42:50,290
Got it?

652
00:42:52,069 --> 00:42:53,114
Hey.

653
00:42:53,114 --> 00:42:57,140
Ha Yeong, I mean, Ha Yeon, wants 10 minutes.

654
00:43:25,090 --> 00:43:26,326
Get inside.

655
00:43:28,150 --> 00:43:29,409
Hey.

656
00:43:29,409 --> 00:43:32,031
It's past four o'clock now, you hear me?

657
00:43:32,697 --> 00:43:36,075
But your brother still hasn't
transferred the money.

658
00:43:36,825 --> 00:43:41,573
And on top of that, you made such a fuss
that we couldn't even undress you!

659
00:43:44,208 --> 00:43:46,926
You're giving us such a hard time.

660
00:43:48,370 --> 00:43:49,515
Miss?

661
00:43:49,515 --> 00:43:52,755
- I can go home and ask my mom to--
- Enough.

662
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:54,674
You wait right here.

663
00:43:54,674 --> 00:43:58,783
I'll let you out once
your brother pays us. Got it?

664
00:43:58,783 --> 00:44:00,721
- What?
- What's wrong?

665
00:44:01,683 --> 00:44:04,322
Want to find out what a true beating is like?

666
00:44:06,104 --> 00:44:08,189
Get in there. Now!

667
00:44:10,329 --> 00:44:11,788
No!

668
00:44:15,072 --> 00:44:16,330
Miss?

669
00:44:16,330 --> 00:44:18,543
Miss!

670
00:44:18,543 --> 00:44:20,235
Is anybody there?

671
00:44:20,235 --> 00:44:21,906
Miss!

672
00:44:50,482 --> 00:44:51,788
Mom!

673
00:44:52,457 --> 00:44:53,970
Why aren't the police coming?

674
00:44:53,970 --> 00:44:55,921
<i>It's been over two hours
since I called the police,</i>

675
00:44:55,921 --> 00:44:57,699
<i>so why isn't anybody here?</i>

676
00:44:57,699 --> 00:44:59,067
J-Jung Yeon!

677
00:44:59,067 --> 00:45:00,905
<i>Why aren't they coming?</i>

678
00:45:02,477 --> 00:45:04,501
<i>You... Are you...</i>

679
00:45:04,501 --> 00:45:06,016
Did you go where Ha Yeon is?

680
00:45:06,016 --> 00:45:07,411
Oh, no, no!

681
00:45:07,411 --> 00:45:09,747
The policeman said that you shouldn't go there!

682
00:45:09,747 --> 00:45:13,530
<i>- Jung Yeon!</i>
- It's just that I can't find her anywhere.

683
00:45:13,530 --> 00:45:16,213
I went to the address she gave me,
but no one was there.

684
00:45:16,213 --> 00:45:20,364
Why would you go there?
That's the police's job!

685
00:45:20,364 --> 00:45:22,418
Get out of there right now!

686
00:45:22,418 --> 00:45:24,186
Do you want to see me lose it?

687
00:45:24,186 --> 00:45:26,287
<i>- Is that it?</i>
- Seriously, Mom!

688
00:45:27,642 --> 00:45:29,435
<i>Mom.</i>

689
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:33,457
Do you know what human trafficking is, Mom?

690
00:45:33,457 --> 00:45:34,654
Do you?

691
00:45:36,692 --> 00:45:39,064
Please, Jung Yeon...

692
00:45:39,064 --> 00:45:41,810
Please just get out of there.

693
00:45:41,810 --> 00:45:43,878
I'm begging you, please!

694
00:45:45,103 --> 00:45:47,652
Do you seriously not care about Ha Yeon at all?

695
00:45:49,169 --> 00:45:51,322
So what if I leave now?

696
00:45:52,237 --> 00:45:54,057
Who will look for her then?

697
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:56,587
The police aren't here.

698
00:45:56,587 --> 00:45:59,023
There's literally nobody here!

699
00:45:59,023 --> 00:46:01,332
So tell me, who's going to find her?

700
00:46:02,050 --> 00:46:04,934
Mom, listen, Mom...

701
00:46:04,934 --> 00:46:07,795
She could be dead, or being sold off!

702
00:46:09,057 --> 00:46:11,522
Are you aware of the situation?

703
00:46:22,430 --> 00:46:24,310
Mommy can't...

704
00:46:24,937 --> 00:46:27,835
I can't do anything...

705
00:46:27,835 --> 00:46:30,850
There's nothing that I can do!

706
00:46:30,850 --> 00:46:33,129
Damn it!

707
00:46:36,037 --> 00:46:37,618
Ha Yeon!

708
00:46:50,009 --> 00:46:52,011
Get me to Gorae Port, please.

709
00:46:55,644 --> 00:46:58,086
Yeah, I remember, too.

710
00:46:58,086 --> 00:46:59,688
Thank goodness, right?

711
00:46:59,688 --> 00:47:03,166
Good afternoon.
We're here following up on a report.

712
00:47:06,566 --> 00:47:07,807
What do you mean?

713
00:47:07,807 --> 00:47:10,122
A girl came here, didn't she?

714
00:47:10,122 --> 00:47:11,401
Where is she?

715
00:47:12,705 --> 00:47:14,540
Hey, mister.

716
00:47:14,540 --> 00:47:17,415
A girl coming into a coffee shop
is hardly illegal.

717
00:47:17,415 --> 00:47:18,566
Mister.

718
00:47:18,566 --> 00:47:20,254
We're a proper establishment.

719
00:47:20,254 --> 00:47:23,719
The girl in question has been reported missing.

720
00:47:23,719 --> 00:47:26,391
We're looking for her right now.

721
00:47:27,764 --> 00:47:31,703
So you expect us to interrogate
every teenager who comes here

722
00:47:31,703 --> 00:47:34,638
and find out if they were
reported missing or not?

723
00:47:34,638 --> 00:47:36,589
Is that what you want?

724
00:47:39,993 --> 00:47:42,825
We're already having a hard time
running this place. You don't need to annoy us.

725
00:47:42,825 --> 00:47:44,236
Ma'am.

726
00:47:44,236 --> 00:47:47,240
We already know what's going on here.

727
00:47:47,240 --> 00:47:49,904
This is a human trafficking ring!

728
00:47:55,167 --> 00:47:56,667
Enough games.

729
00:47:56,667 --> 00:47:58,403
Where is she?

730
00:47:58,403 --> 00:48:01,673
Confess, and we'll give you leniency
on your sentence.

731
00:48:01,673 --> 00:48:03,808
Look at you, big guy, with your big words.

732
00:48:03,808 --> 00:48:06,388
Mister, do you have proof?

733
00:48:06,388 --> 00:48:08,798
Do you see any proof lying around?

734
00:48:08,798 --> 00:48:10,494
Is being a detective such a big deal?

735
00:48:10,494 --> 00:48:13,020
Yes, in fact, it is a big deal.

736
00:48:18,775 --> 00:48:20,810
Hey, there's a tunnel here. Let's go.

737
00:48:20,810 --> 00:48:22,966
Get him!

738
00:48:22,966 --> 00:48:24,570
- Check it out.
- Yes, sir.

739
00:48:26,365 --> 00:48:29,406
It's not what you think!

740
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:30,835
Hey.

741
00:48:30,835 --> 00:48:32,303
Hey!

742
00:48:34,760 --> 00:48:36,539
You brutes are crossing the line!

743
00:48:36,539 --> 00:48:38,947
Dropped the polite act, have you?

744
00:48:38,947 --> 00:48:40,723
She's not here, damn it.

745
00:48:40,723 --> 00:48:42,500
I said she's not goddamn here!

746
00:48:42,500 --> 00:48:45,047
In my thirteen years of being a detective,

747
00:48:45,047 --> 00:48:48,147
I've never had a case
where those words were actually true.

748
00:48:48,147 --> 00:48:49,939
Kim Ha Yeon!

749
00:48:50,606 --> 00:48:52,325
Where are you?

750
00:48:54,439 --> 00:48:55,477
Hey.

751
00:48:55,477 --> 00:48:57,233
We're in trouble. Get here fast.

752
00:49:04,693 --> 00:49:07,072
Miss, my brother said he sent the money!

753
00:49:07,072 --> 00:49:08,612
Miss!

754
00:49:12,274 --> 00:49:13,833
Hi, little Missy.

755
00:49:20,169 --> 00:49:21,514
Who are you?

756
00:49:21,514 --> 00:49:24,170
Where's the lady?
My brother says he sent the money.

757
00:49:24,170 --> 00:49:25,800
Hey, you.

758
00:49:25,800 --> 00:49:27,426
I thought you didn't have your phone.

759
00:49:27,426 --> 00:49:29,962
How do you know if he sent the money or not?

760
00:49:33,432 --> 00:49:34,644
I mean...

761
00:49:45,903 --> 00:49:47,179
Ha Yeon!

762
00:49:48,073 --> 00:49:49,382
Kim Ha Yeon!

763
00:50:00,454 --> 00:50:02,104
Ha Yeon!

764
00:50:06,201 --> 00:50:07,328
Missy.

765
00:50:08,133 --> 00:50:09,760
Did you call the police?

766
00:50:09,760 --> 00:50:13,117
No, how would I do that?
I genuinely don't have a phone, and...

767
00:50:13,117 --> 00:50:16,926
You used a payphone, right?
Did you call the police with it?

768
00:50:16,926 --> 00:50:18,502
No, I swear I didn't!

769
00:50:18,502 --> 00:50:20,166
Hey!

770
00:50:20,166 --> 00:50:22,934
You really messed things up for us, you know!

771
00:50:22,934 --> 00:50:27,486
If you want to die, just do it!
Why would you call the police?

772
00:50:27,486 --> 00:50:29,081
Come here, you.

773
00:50:29,947 --> 00:50:31,851
Grab her, come on!

774
00:50:33,027 --> 00:50:36,506
- But I swear I didn't call the police!
- Come here!

775
00:50:47,066 --> 00:50:48,223
Ha Yeon!

776
00:50:48,223 --> 00:50:49,759
What? What's wrong?

777
00:50:50,820 --> 00:50:52,511
Run!

778
00:50:52,511 --> 00:50:53,907
You bastard!

779
00:50:55,010 --> 00:50:56,946
Move, you bastard!

780
00:50:56,946 --> 00:50:58,508
Go, run!

781
00:51:02,271 --> 00:51:03,298
Go!

782
00:51:03,298 --> 00:51:05,107
- Go!
- Grab her!

783
00:51:05,107 --> 00:51:06,552
Run!

784
00:51:10,779 --> 00:51:12,278
Wait, wait.

785
00:51:12,278 --> 00:51:13,320
I'm a policeman.

786
00:51:13,320 --> 00:51:15,593
We're the police, yes.

787
00:51:15,593 --> 00:51:17,562
- Are you okay?
- H-help me.

788
00:51:17,562 --> 00:51:19,413
Help me, sir, please!

789
00:51:19,413 --> 00:51:20,914
Help me...

790
00:51:20,914 --> 00:51:22,730
I'm here, please! I'm locked in here!

791
00:51:22,730 --> 00:51:24,152
Help me, I'm here! Mister!

792
00:51:24,152 --> 00:51:26,292
You, ask for backup.

793
00:51:26,292 --> 00:51:28,226
Things just got serious.

794
00:51:28,226 --> 00:51:30,159
- Wait just a little longer.
- Okay.

795
00:51:38,033 --> 00:51:39,610
Captain, sir!

796
00:52:18,427 --> 00:52:19,614
Answer me. Say it.

797
00:52:19,614 --> 00:52:21,642
I said, answer me!

798
00:52:21,642 --> 00:52:23,134
Come here.

799
00:52:23,810 --> 00:52:24,931
Hey, scumbag!

800
00:52:24,931 --> 00:52:27,352
- Police!
- Get him!

801
00:52:27,352 --> 00:52:28,573
Stop there!

802
00:52:28,573 --> 00:52:30,510
- This is the police!
- Hey, are you okay?

803
00:52:30,510 --> 00:52:31,602
Sir!

804
00:52:31,602 --> 00:52:32,905
Hey!

805
00:52:32,905 --> 00:52:37,192
[Ambulance]

806
00:52:38,659 --> 00:52:40,814
You can't do this!

807
00:52:42,133 --> 00:52:44,639
- It hurts!
- You scumbag!

808
00:52:52,106 --> 00:52:53,781
Stay still!

809
00:52:57,093 --> 00:52:58,773
I didn't!

810
00:52:59,983 --> 00:53:01,011
Detective, sir!

811
00:53:01,011 --> 00:53:02,073
Where's Ha Yeon?

812
00:53:02,073 --> 00:53:03,882
We haven't found her yet.

813
00:53:03,882 --> 00:53:05,289
I'm sorry.

814
00:53:22,120 --> 00:53:23,521
<i>That day...</i>

815
00:53:24,620 --> 00:53:28,152
<i>The morning battered my face
with droplets of rain,</i>

816
00:53:29,733 --> 00:53:31,720
<i>and that sea...</i>

817
00:53:31,720 --> 00:53:34,086
<i>Its briny smell carried more salt than ever.</i>

818
00:53:56,907 --> 00:53:59,945
<i>Past the scent of men I cannot name,</i>

819
00:54:00,988 --> 00:54:05,012
<i>and the stench of the sewers
filling the alleyway,</i>

820
00:54:06,368 --> 00:54:11,705
<i>I am greeted by the sky, blue as ever,
and the wailing cicadas.</i>

821
00:54:27,181 --> 00:54:30,040
<i>When I turned to look behind me,</i>

822
00:54:30,040 --> 00:54:34,728
<i>I was standing in a different world,
a world unlike mine.</i>

823
00:54:44,754 --> 00:54:45,923
Ha Yeon.

824
00:55:26,674 --> 00:55:29,004
I told you I'd wait at the lighthouse.

825
00:55:30,980 --> 00:55:32,371
<i>And...</i>

826
00:55:33,220 --> 00:55:36,136
<i>of all the summers that I would meet,</i>

827
00:55:36,999 --> 00:55:39,819
<i>the sole, most unforgettable summer,</i>

828
00:55:39,819 --> 00:55:42,064
<i>the one and only summer...</i>

829
00:55:44,835 --> 00:55:46,302
<i>was starting,</i>

830
00:55:48,053 --> 00:55:50,748
<i>for us.</i>
